    <Placemark>
      <name>Acre (עכו)</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<h3>Acre (עכו)</h3>
<p><b>Period:</b> 10. Classical &amp; Later Periods (-586 to +638 CE)</p>
<p><b>Installation Type:</b> Aqueduct Channel</p>
<p><b>Location Precision:</b> Tier 1: High Precision (Pinpoint Well/Installation &lt; 50m)</p>
<p><b>Region:</b> Coastal Plain</p>
<p><b>Dissertation Reference:</b> §3.7 (Pages 212)</p>
<hr/>
<p><b>Archaeological Description (10. Classical &amp; Later Periods):</b></p>
<p>A Hellenistic aqueduct consisting of tunnels and shafts, approximately 13 km long, built in the 3rd century BCE.</p>]]></description>
