    <Placemark>
      <name>Rome (Aqua Marcia) (רומא (אקווה מרקיה))</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<h3>Rome (Aqua Marcia) (רומא (אקווה מרקיה))</h3>
<p><b>Period:</b> 10. Classical &amp; Later Periods (-586 to +638 CE)</p>
<p><b>Installation Type:</b> Aqueduct Channel</p>
<p><b>Location Precision:</b> Tier 4: International Comparative Site (&lt; 100m - 1km)</p>
<p><b>Region:</b> Italy</p>
<p><b>Dissertation Reference:</b> §3.7 (Pages 211)</p>
<hr/>
<p><b>Archaeological Description (10. Classical &amp; Later Periods):</b></p>
<p>The Aqua Marcia, an aqueduct 91 km long (10 km on arches), built between 144-140 BCE, supplying water to Rome.</p>]]></description>
